NOTE:

directory sue_fixed contains the schematics with fixed size fets.

directory sue_param contains the schematics with parameterizable
fet sizes - THIS IS THE DIRECTORY that has been modified by
pat so the cells can be routed.

The cell library includes:

	gds for each cell
	lef for each cell
	timing library in .lib format
	verilog behavioral model for each cell
	spice netlist of each cell

Proposed 0.18 um TSMC cell library characteristics:

	Metal pitch (M1-M5)	0.74 um
		square surrounds
		stacked vias ok without any additional work

	cell height		10 grids

	Route on offset of 0.5 grids in X, Y.

	Power (vdd, gnd) in M1, 1.0 um wide (shared)

	Well and Substrate ties along top and bottom borders

	minimum layout grid 0.01 um

Process characteristics:

	Minimum routable contacted pitch: 0.66 (square grid)
				or	  0.56 x 0.66

	Minimum pitch that allows all stacked vias: 0.73 um

	Fet pitch	0.72 um.

	Minimum fet with:
		1 contact:	0.42 um
		2 contacts:	0.89 um
		3 contacts:	1.36 um

Micro Magic cell library characteristics:

	P:N ratio 2:1

	Five different size cells: A,B,C,D,E
		Strength corresponds to output drive strength, thus a
		INVC, AND2C, MUX2C all have the same drive strength but
		have different input capacitances and intrinsic delays.

		E = 2xD, D = 2xC, C = 2xB, B = 2xA

	Larger cells would break electromigration limits for min. wires.
	(really maximum current, not electromigration).

	Not all sizes for all cells.  Typically, the more inputs,
	the fewer sizes.

	for 0.18 um, 0.74 um grid, 10 grid height:

		A size output: 0.92/0.46 (p/n)
		B size output: 1.84/0.92
		C size output: 3.68/1.84
		...
	
		Maximum transistor height before folding: 2.35 um

